The graph shows Marco's pay $P$ (\$) for $h$ hours of casual work.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$h$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$P$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,0) {$2$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {$4$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,0) {$6$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,0) {$8$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$44$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,2) {$88$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,3) {$132$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,4) {$176$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,4);


\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which equation relates $P$ and $h$?

The graph shows the fuel $F$ (litres) used by a delivery van after driving a distance $d$ (km).
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$d$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$F$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,0) {$100$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {$200$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,0) {$300$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,0) {$400$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$7$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,2) {$14$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,3) {$21$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,4) {$28$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,4);


\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
What does the gradient of this graph represent?

Two graphs, $A$ and $B$, are shown below.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\begin{scope}
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,12);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{km};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,12.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{\$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,3)--(4,11);
\fill (0,3) circle (2.2pt);
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (-0.1,3) {\$3};
\node[font=\small] at (2,-1.3) {$A$: Taxi fare};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(7,0)}]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,12);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{kg};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,12.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{\$};
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(4,12);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[font=\small] at (2,-1.3) {$B$: Cost of oranges};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which graph shows direct variation?

A market stall owner graphs two of her costs, labelled $A$ and $B$ below, against different quantities.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.55]
\begin{scope}
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,16);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{kg};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,16.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{\$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,0)--(4,16);
\fill (0,0) circle (2.2pt);
\node[font=\small] at (2,-1.3) {$A$: Cost of bananas};
\end{scope}
\begin{scope}[shift={(7,0)}]
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{runners};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{min};
\draw[thick,blue,domain=0.5:4,samples=40,smooth,variable=\x] plot ({\x},{1.8/\x+0.3});
\node[font=\small] at (2,-1.3) {$B$: Time per lap};
\end{scope}
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Only one of these is an example of direct variation. Which one, and what feature of its graph tells you?

The graph shows axes for the cost $C$ (\$) of buying pears of weight $w$ (kg), with four labelled points.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$w$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$C$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,0) {$1$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {$2$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,0) {$3$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$8$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,2) {$16$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,3) {$24$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,4) {$32$};

\fill (2,2) circle (2.2pt);\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (2,2) {$A$};\fill (2,1.25) circle (2.2pt);\node[below right,font=\footnotesize] at (2,1.25) {$B$};\fill (3,3.375) circle (2.2pt);\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (3,3.375) {$C$};\fill (0,1) circle (2.2pt);\node[above left,font=\footnotesize] at (0,1) {$D$};

\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which labelled point could lie on the graph of $C = 8w$?

