The graph shows the pay earned by two workers, $C$ and $D$, for the same number of hours worked.
[tikz]
\begin{tikzpicture}[scale=0.6]
\draw[step=1,gray!25,very thin] (0,0) grid (4,4);
\draw[->] (0,0)--(4.5,0) node[right,font=\scriptsize]{$h$};
\draw[->] (0,0)--(0,4.5) node[above,font=\scriptsize]{$P$};
\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (1,0) {$1$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (2,0) {$2$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (3,0) {$3$};\node[below,font=\scriptsize] at (4,0) {$4$};
\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,1) {$18$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,2) {$36$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,3) {$54$};\node[left,font=\scriptsize] at (0,4) {$72$};

\fill (3,2) circle (2.2pt);\node[below right,font=\footnotesize] at (3,2) {$C$};\fill (3,3) circle (2.2pt);\node[above right,font=\footnotesize] at (3,3) {$D$};
\draw[thick,red] (0,0)--(3,2);
\draw[thick,blue] (0,0)--(3,3);
\end{tikzpicture}
[/tikz]
Which worker earns at the higher hourly rate?
